Can somebody offer me some advice....or point me in the right direction? 
Thanks in advance:

I need some way to limit where a paticular user account can log in.  I need
to set up this account so if the user logs in at an unauthorized location
they get kicked right out.  If they log in at an acceptable location a
program executes based on where they are.....

This is part of a custom point-of-sale "debit" system and I only want the
account logging in at the foodservice locations (for obvious reasons).

I had this witking under LAT where I used statements such as the
following.....

$ !
$ if f$getdvi("tt:","tt_accpornam") .eqs. "THUB05/PORT_12" then goto flex_m
$ if f$getdvi("tt:","tt_accpornam") .eqs. "THUB05/PORT_14" then goto flex_s
$ if f$getdvi("tt:","tt_accpornam") .eqs. "THUB05/PORT_15" then goto flex_d
$ goto no_good

Well, our IT area is discontinuing the LAT protocol so I need to somehow do
this through TELNET - TCP/IP.  When I use the f$getdvi function with the
new protocol all I am able to get is the terminal server address (such as
thub05.sample.edu).....what I need is some way to identify the port number
that I am connected to (i.e. :4020.....we've already set it so it does not
change, thus we can validate against it).  I'm also open to a totally
different approach for limiting this access!

Any thoughts?  Suggestions? Alternatives?

Thank you,

Dave Carpentiere
Plymouth State College



